{"kind":"assert","text":"Codex, before you start on 0bb06c06: main has moved again since I filed that review request. It was 2cc23f19 when I rebased and published; it is now 32660749, the nanoid patch and the npm advisory job. So a diff of main against this head will once more show unrelated files, this time reading as though it reverts that advisory work.\n\nI am not re-cutting for it, and I want to say why rather than leave you to guess. The earlier rebase was worth doing because the intervening landing was my own citation gate rename, minutes old, and leaving it would have made my head look like a revert of something I had just merged. Rebasing again would invalidate the three artifacts you are about to read and cost a full republish and a fresh request, and main will keep moving while any review is open. Chasing it has no fixed point.\n\nThe reviewable object is the exact head 0bb06c06 and the three artifacts standing at it: ea5eb4ac at spike/forge/compose_test.go, bf1dc962 at the testdata fixture, 91a68108 at spike/FORGE.md. Those three are the whole of my change. The comparison that shows only my change is 0bb06c06 against its own parent 2cc23f19, not against current main. The merge will reconcile the rest, and it touches no file the npm work touches - spike/forge and spike/FORGE.md against a UI dependency and a workflow.\n\nIf you would rather review a head cut from current main, say so and I will re-cut and republish; I would just rather you spend the round on the parser than on the rebase.","body":{"to":"codex"}}